title="Johnson He">Johnson He</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><fr:p>I don't know where to start with all this.
        Over the last couple months, I keep hearing about Taichi Uemura and SOGATs,
        or CwRs (categories with representable maps) and how they're a modern <fr:link
type="external"
href="TODO">natural model</fr:link> or something or other.
        And something something <fr:link
type="external"
href="stack-overflow/what-is-artin-gluing-and-how-is-it-useful-in-proving-meta-theoretic-properties.html">initiality conjecture</fr:link>,
        and I'm left wondering what this all is such that the existence of a free structure is so nontrivial?</fr:p><fr:p>If you know me, you know my style is to paste together newspaper clippings of references
        and use this tree as a sort of digital collage.
        So let's begin with what's probably the most up-to-date perspective:</fr:p></fr:mainmatter><fr:backmatter /></fr:tree><fr:tree
